WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:14.455
"I can't go back to Magica!"

2
00:00:14.795 --> 00:00:15.635
Zann blurted out.

3
00:00:16.536 --> 00:00:18.237
"Not without finding my parents."

4
00:00:19.297 --> 00:00:21.759
"Don't be a fool, boy," Wyssa snapped.

5
00:00:21.779 --> 00:00:25.281
"I know I can find them," Zann retorted.

6
00:00:25.301 --> 00:00:28.062
"I even have a clue—World X.

7
00:00:29.163 --> 00:00:31.024
I know my parents wanted to find it.

8
00:00:31.912 --> 00:00:34.633
Maybe that's where they are—they could be trapped there!"

9
00:00:35.733 --> 00:00:36.733
Wyssa looked startled.

10
00:00:36.753 --> 00:00:42.295
"How do you know about— never mind," she said, interrupting herself.

11
00:00:43.295 --> 00:00:45.876
"Yes, it's true they wanted to find World X.

12
00:00:46.356 --> 00:00:48.196
But I have no idea where it is.

13
00:00:49.117 --> 00:00:54.478
I promise I'll try to find out—after you and your friends are safely back in Magica."

14
00:00:54.498 --> 00:00:58.039
"That sounds like a good offer, Zann," Gliss said.

15
00:00:58.999 --> 00:01:02.060
Ignoring her, Zann glared at Wyssa.

16
00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:04.142
"They're my parents," he said.

17
00:01:04.162 --> 00:01:07.424
"Nobody cares about finding them as much as I do!"

18
00:01:08.705 --> 00:01:11.988
"I'm not so sure about that, boy," Wyssa muttered.

19
00:01:12.008 --> 00:01:16.472
"Morb is—" Once again she stopped herself.

20
00:01:16.492 --> 00:01:19.034
"Morb?" Perda spoke up.

21
00:01:19.554 --> 00:01:21.195
"What does he have to do with this?"

22
00:01:21.215 --> 00:01:22.456
"Forget it.

23
00:01:22.957 --> 00:01:24.058
I shouldn't have said anything."

24
00:01:24.898 --> 00:01:26.780
Wyssa stalked off toward the wormhole.

25
00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:27.721
"Let's go."

26
00:01:28.701 --> 00:01:31.624
"Not until you tell me what's going on," Zann said.

27
00:01:32.476 --> 00:01:33.797
"Why did you mention Morb?

28
00:01:34.377 --> 00:01:36.158
Is he looking for my parents too?"

29
00:01:37.399 --> 00:01:39.460
Wyssa scowled and then sighed.

30
00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:41.741
"I suppose you deserve to know.

31
00:01:42.702 --> 00:01:45.663
Maybe it will convince you not to rush off by yourself.

32
00:01:46.864 --> 00:01:49.745
Yes, I've heard rumors that Morb is looking for your parents.

33
00:01:50.626 --> 00:01:51.626
Nobody knows why."

34
00:01:52.727 --> 00:01:53.588
Zann froze.

35
00:01:54.008 --> 00:01:56.829
What could Morb possibly want with Zann's parents?

36
00:01:56.849 --> 00:01:59.131
"Hold on," Perda said.

37
00:01:59.151 --> 00:02:01.532
"How can Morb be searching for anyone?

38
00:02:02.324 --> 00:02:05.527
I thought he went back to being a Void when Zann defeated him."

39
00:02:06.868 --> 00:02:10.271
"I don't know how he's able to use the wormholes," Wyssa said.

40
00:02:10.291 --> 00:02:13.593
"But he's not keeping his search a secret."

41
00:02:14.614 --> 00:02:15.175
She grimaced.

42
00:02:15.715 --> 00:02:18.898
"He's left a trail of terrified worlds behind him."

43
00:02:19.678 --> 00:02:21.020
Perda's eyes widened.

44
00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:25.623
"That must be why the Skellians freaked out when we mentioned Morb's name!"

45
00:02:25.643 --> 00:02:28.506
"Whatever," Zann said to Wyssa.

46
00:02:28.526 --> 00:02:31.008
"I'm still not going back to Magica."

47
00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:37.042
He rubbed both hands on his legs, hoping this spell would work.

48
00:02:37.923 --> 00:02:41.325
Touching the trunk of a sturdy tree, he cried, "Shackle!"

49
00:02:42.406 --> 00:02:42.806
It worked!

50
00:02:43.407 --> 00:02:46.148
Magical shackles appeared, binding Zann to the tree.

51
00:02:46.989 --> 00:02:48.130
Wyssa gnashed her teeth.

52
00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:50.351
"Stop this foolishness!

53
00:02:51.212 --> 00:02:54.294
Remove those shackles at once, or I'll do it for you."

54
00:02:54.314 --> 00:02:56.695
"You can't," Perda said.

55
00:02:56.715 --> 00:02:59.677
"Nobody can remove another person's Shackle spell."

56
00:03:00.878 --> 00:03:01.499
"She's right.

57
00:03:01.819 --> 00:03:04.272
And you won't change my mind," Zann said.

58
00:03:04.292 --> 00:03:08.213
"Take my friends home, and then we can search together.

59
00:03:09.113 --> 00:03:10.634
Otherwise I'll search on my own."

60
00:03:10.654 --> 00:03:13.855
"You don't know what you're doing, boy."

61
00:03:14.435 --> 00:03:16.435
Wyssa narrowed her eyes at Zann.

62
00:03:16.455 --> 00:03:23.037
"If even half the rumors about Morb's new powers are true, you won't have a chance against him."

63
00:03:24.698 --> 00:03:25.698
Zann stared at her.

64
00:03:26.138 --> 00:03:29.619
"You can't make me do anything," he said defiantly.

65
00:03:29.639 --> 00:03:33.020
"You didn't even know when Morb was tricking you!"

66
00:03:34.016 --> 00:03:35.177
"What are you talking about?"

67
00:03:35.397 --> 00:03:36.117
Wyssa demanded.

68
00:03:36.137 --> 00:03:42.961
"When you sent my parents off course with that scatter beast, it wasn't an accident," said Zann.

69
00:03:42.981 --> 00:03:45.502
"It was part of Morb's plan.

70
00:03:45.842 --> 00:03:47.283
He told me so himself."

71
00:03:48.944 --> 00:03:50.285
Wyssa's eyes went wide.

72
00:03:50.305 --> 00:03:54.607
"What?" Her yell echoed through the quiet forest.

73
00:03:55.488 --> 00:03:58.349
She leaped forward and touched Zann's forehead.

74
00:03:58.369 --> 00:04:01.070
"Truth!" she intoned.

75
00:04:01.091 --> 00:04:06.145
"Ow!" Zann yelped as he felt a sizzling sensation in his head.

76
00:04:07.025 --> 00:04:11.926
A second later Wyssa backed away, her eyes burning with rage.

77
00:04:11.946 --> 00:04:16.367
"So it is true," she said through gritted teeth.

78
00:04:16.387 --> 00:04:23.689
"I've been torturing myself all these years, thinking I was to blame for your parents' disappearance.

79
00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:26.830
Morb will pay for this!"

80
00:04:28.151 --> 00:04:30.371
Alarmed, Zann glanced at his friends.

81
00:04:31.151 --> 00:04:33.192
They were all staring at Wyssa in silence.

82
00:04:34.096 --> 00:04:35.677
Zing cowered behind Darb.

83
00:04:36.538 --> 00:04:38.039
Wyssa swept toward Zann again.

84
00:04:38.059 --> 00:04:39.840
"Release!" she said.

85
00:04:40.601 --> 00:04:41.762
The shackles exploded.

86
00:04:42.702 --> 00:04:43.463
Zann gasped.

87
00:04:43.483 --> 00:04:48.286
"How did you—" Before he could finish, Wyssa grabbed Gliss.

88
00:04:49.127 --> 00:04:51.689
"You're in charge now, Red," Wyssa said.

89
00:04:51.709 --> 00:04:56.813
"Take Zann and these others straight back to Magica."

90
00:04:56.833 --> 00:04:59.074
"I I Gliss stammered.

91
00:04:59.575 --> 00:05:01.216
She seemed too scared to speak.

92
00:05:02.304 --> 00:05:05.625
"This will ensure that you follow my orders, girl."

93
00:05:06.626 --> 00:05:08.627
Wyssa put her hands over Gliss' face.

94
00:05:09.387 --> 00:05:14.129
When the old woman pulled them away, glowing purple goggles covered Gliss' eyes.

95
00:05:14.149 --> 00:05:18.311
"Those goggles will show you the way," Wyssa said.

96
00:05:18.331 --> 00:05:22.492
"They'll also provide extra magic for navigating the vortex.

97
00:05:23.473 --> 00:05:29.975
But don't try to remove them until all of you are safely back in Magica, or you'll suffer

98
00:05:30.055 --> 00:05:31.236
intense pain."

99
00:05:32.664 --> 00:05:35.485
"I I understand," Gliss said.

100
00:05:35.505 --> 00:05:40.546
"Good." Wyssa leaped for the wormhole.

101
00:05:40.566 --> 00:05:43.287
"Revenge will be mine!"

102
00:05:43.587 --> 00:05:44.967
she cried as she disappeared.

103
00:05:44.987 --> 00:05:48.909
"Wow," Perda said, her voice shaking.

104
00:05:48.929 --> 00:05:50.809
"That was scary!"

105
00:05:51.729 --> 00:05:54.470
Zann nodded, no longer doubting Wyssa's power.

106
00:05:55.390 --> 00:05:57.231
For a moment they all stayed quiet.

107
00:05:57.251 --> 00:06:01.052
"Maybe Wyssa is right," Zann thought.

108
00:06:01.512 --> 00:06:06.235
Maybe it was better to let her handle the search Finally Gliss spoke up.

109
00:06:06.255 --> 00:06:08.977
"Zann, what do you want me to do?"

110
00:06:09.958 --> 00:06:11.839
Zann turned to her and sighed.

111
00:06:11.859 --> 00:06:14.401
"It's not like we have much choice."

112
00:06:14.421 --> 00:06:16.783
"There's always a choice."

113
00:06:17.703 --> 00:06:20.585
Gliss took a deep breath and reached for the goggles.

114
00:06:20.605 --> 00:06:22.947
"No!" Darb cried.

115
00:06:22.967 --> 00:06:24.908
"Gliss!" said Zann.

116
00:06:24.928 --> 00:06:27.790
"You don't have to—" "Aah!"

117
00:06:28.090 --> 00:06:30.272
cried Gliss, ripping the goggles from her face.

118
00:06:31.048 --> 00:06:34.350
She collapsed on the ground, writhing and crying out in pain.

119
00:06:35.711 --> 00:06:36.851
Darb rushed over to her.

120
00:06:38.232 --> 00:06:40.854
A minute later she was able to climb back to her feet.

121
00:06:40.874 --> 00:06:43.855
"Th—there," Gliss said.

122
00:06:43.876 --> 00:06:48.718
"If you want to continue your search, I won't stop you.

123
00:06:49.239 --> 00:06:51.160
In fact I'll come along."

124
00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:53.241
Perda looked at Zann.

125
00:06:53.561 --> 00:06:54.422
"We all will."

126
00:06:55.502 --> 00:06:56.203
Zann gulped.

127
00:06:56.603 --> 00:06:58.364
Putting himself in danger was one thing.

128
00:06:59.180 --> 00:07:01.502
But could he also risk his friends' lives again?

129
00:07:01.522 --> 00:07:03.524
"Are you sure?"

130
00:07:03.864 --> 00:07:04.325
he asked.

131
00:07:05.185 --> 00:07:07.187
Gliss, Perda, and Darb nodded.

132
00:07:07.968 --> 00:07:09.469
Zing let out an excited whistle.

133
00:07:10.330 --> 00:07:11.871
Zann suddenly felt braver.

134
00:07:12.451 --> 00:07:14.834
He and his friends had defeated Morb once before.

135
00:07:15.634 --> 00:07:18.977
They made a powerful team, the kind of team that could do anything.

136
00:07:19.898 --> 00:07:21.139
"Okay," he told them.

137
00:07:21.559 --> 00:07:22.140
"Let's go!"
